                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "7cd8f860-f66e-4f74-abf0-3de9015b44cd",
                        "entry_id": "5711b85e-7ac7-3bca-a9c6-ae4445715664",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "регрессио́нны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "be950fb9-4cf0-398d-8c4a-1a58f0f13df9",
                        "entry_id": "5711b85e-7ac7-3bca-a9c6-ae4445715664",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем. связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным регрессия; связанный с применением регрессии в математической статистике"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fba0fdea-a4a9-4949-b153-8f79b5e59607",
                                "sense_id": "be950fb9-4cf0-398d-8c4a-1a58f0f13df9",
                                "text": "Исследование данных о тренде ОСО за 70 лет (1926 — 1996 гг.) с использованием метода множественного регрессионного анализа, учитывающего 11-летние циклы солнечной активности и выбросы вулканического аэрозоля, дало среднюю величину убыли общего содержания озона с 1970 по 1996 год 1,9+0,6% за десятилетие, т. е. менее 0,2% в год."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23bab2d6-9d9c-4aea-ac24-ac2faf000e40",
                        "source_entry_id": "5711b85e-7ac7-3bca-a9c6-ae4445715664",
                        "source_sense_id": "be950fb9-4cf0-398d-8c4a-1a58f0f13df9",
                        "target_lang_word": "regression",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "regression",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7afc206c-232a-34c8-904c-ce82d529676d",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An action of regressing, a return to a previous state."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4813f70-6bda-40e0-97d3-aeef5e0275d3",
                                                "sense_id": "7afc206c-232a-34c8-904c-ce82d529676d",
                                                "text": "Few of these groups or communities that are classed as \"savage\" show no traces of regression from a more advanced cultural stage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6dff488f-28f6-33ff-b102-3fcd07a3ecdc",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An action of travelling mentally back in time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7008d568-5849-4e3b-9769-0fd2a90c2118",
                                                "sense_id": "6dff488f-28f6-33ff-b102-3fcd07a3ecdc",
                                                "text": "I have done past life regressions on my own through self-hypnosis techniques that I learned in Brian Weiss's book Many Lives, Many Masters as well as with past life regression tapes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "afab6ff1-2282-3812-8277-a60a16e8ab3b",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A psychotherapeutic method whereby healing is facilitated by inducing the patient to act out behaviour typical of an earlier developmental stage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7085b1ff-0605-30a6-8258-dc9a4e01f7ed",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An analytic method to measure the association of one or more independent variables with a dependent variable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "714a24d8-959d-439d-b369-68d3d75f6a6a",
                                                "sense_id": "7085b1ff-0605-30a6-8258-dc9a4e01f7ed",
                                                "text": "A social norm hypothesis [of crime] that focuses on the social meaning of order cannot be tested by a single time frame regression of neighborhood disorder and crime. That is simply asking too much of the data."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b32dfb2-c08f-48d2-8b43-fc1bd1c925ad",
                                                "sense_id": "7085b1ff-0605-30a6-8258-dc9a4e01f7ed",
                                                "text": "Supervised learning problems are categorized into \"regression\" and \"classification\" problems. In a regression problem, we are trying to predict results within a continuous output, meaning that we are trying to map input variables to some continuous function."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c10cab4-0b8d-359f-849b-265748e22d79",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An equation using specified and associated data for two or more variables such that one variable can be estimated from the remaining variable(s)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "719d8606-9030-37ed-80e1-b195060e8e6f",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The reappearance of a bug in a piece of software that had previously been fixed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa9d593c-62b2-3672-bfcc-e93de1e7a6e6",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The diminishing of a cellular mass like a tumor, or of an organ size."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "651496a4-35ce-31d2-8a48-762baa4745d8",
                                        "entry_id": "a91764ca-719b-3736-aa1c-4dba596da8b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The making an exercise less straining to perform by manipulating the details of its performance like loaded weight, range of motion, angle, speed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
